    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Complete edentulism with an implant-retained lower overdenture (K08.103)</content>. A successful two-implant overdenture: firm retention, chewing 8 of 10 and clear speech. [S]<list><item>Prosthodontic recall every year, with radiographs of the implants at the first recall.</item><item>Replace the attachment inserts when retention falls, often every year or two.</item><item>Continue daily cleaning and overnight removal.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Unintended weight loss with nutritional risk (R63.4)</content>. Resolved: weight up 2.4 kg to 94.8 kg on a full diet, albumin 4.1 g/dL; the MNA-SF of 12 counts the pneumonia as a recent illness. [S]<list><item>Weight at routine visits.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Oral mucosal examination and oral cancer screening (lips, cheeks, tongue, floor of mouth, palate, ridges, neck nodes)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Denture fit: retention, stability, occlusion, vertical dimension and sore spots</td><td>At diagnosis, 24 hours to one week after delivery, after each adjustment, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Planned check four days after attachment pick-up kept, no adjustment needed; today firm retention, stable, even occlusion</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Implant sites and peri-implant mucosa</td><td>One to two weeks after surgery, at attachment connection, then at each review and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Peri-implant mucosa healthy without bleeding; attachments clean</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Radiographs of the implants</td><td>At the first yearly recall, then as indicated</td><td>Due</td><td>At the first prosthodontic recall</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>94.8 kg, up 2.4 kg from intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Nutrition screen (MNA-SF, recorded as narrative)</td><td>At baseline when at risk, after about three months, and at six months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>MNA-SF 12 of 14 (normal): food intake 2, weight loss 3, mobility 2, recent illness 0 (pneumonia), neuropsychological 2, BMI 3</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Albumin</td><td>At baseline and at six months when at nutritional risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4.1 g/dL, from 3.7 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Chewing and speech (patient-rated chewing ability out of 10; clarity of speech in reading aloud)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Chewing 8 of 10; speeches without the denture moving</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Denture hygiene: daily cleaning, dentures out overnight, ridge and tongue cleaning; attachment cleaning</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily cleaning of dentures and attachments; out overnight</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Prosthodontic recall</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>First recall in one year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Oral ulcers healed within two weeks of relieving the denture, without need for a biopsy. Outcome by 1790-02-02: Both ulcers healed at two weeks; no biopsy needed [S]</item><item>New complete dentures that are comfortable and stable for eating and speaking. Outcome by 1790-04-13: Delivered six weeks before the twelve-week review; one adjustment; no sore spots now [S]</item><item>A two-implant lower overdenture in function. Outcome by 1790-07-13: Two implants integrated; stud attachments connected three weeks before the six-month review [S]</item><item>Regain weight and a normal nutrition screen. Outcome by 1790-07-13: Weight 92.4 to 94.8 kg; MNA-SF 10 to 12; albumin 3.7 to 4.1 g/dL [S]</item><item>Speak in public without the lower denture moving. Outcome by 1790-07-13: No lifting or clicking during speeches since the attachments were connected [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Recombinant zoster vaccine, second of two doses [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evidence-based guidelines for the care and maintenance of complete dentures: a publication of the American College of Prosthodontists (2011); The McGill consensus statement on overdentures. Mandibular two-implant overdentures as first choice standard of care for edentulous patients (2002); The York consensus statement on implant-supported overdentures (2009); Evidence-based clinical practice guideline for the evaluation of potentially malignant disorders in the oral cavity: A report of the American Dental Association (2017); Validation of the Mini Nutritional Assessment short-form (MNA-SF): a practical tool for identification of nutritional status (2009); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Second recombinant zoster dose given today. Prosthodontic recall in one year. Preventive visit in eight months. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
